# T04 TeraDesk via #Z (sd-tera): the rebuilt DESKTOP.NAP (gemlib.a with the
# 32-bit *_long accessors + the six pointer-count overlays; the linked
# TeraDesk differs from the pre-T04 binary in ONE instruction, mt_wind_get's
# IN_LEN for WF_NAME/WF_INFO = 6, a path TeraDesk never takes). What the run
# observes is TeraDesk's resource.c:307-315 menu trimming: with
# `mnsize >= buffer.size` TeraDesk deletes 13 entries (SEP1-9, MDELETE,
# MFCOPY, MSHSIZ, MREVS) from the File / View / Options boxes.
# A: idle. File title (88,8) -> B: File box. Slide to View (135,8) -> C: View
# box. Slide to Options (260,8) -> D: Options box. Out (400,300) + click =
# cancel, park -> E.
200 parkbr
1000 arm
1100 mark A_IDLE
1400 move 88 8
1900 mark B_FILE_OPEN
2200 move 135 8
2700 mark C_VIEW_OPEN
3000 move 260 8
3500 mark D_OPTIONS_OPEN
3800 move 400 300
4100 down
4103 up
4600 parkbr
5100 mark E_CLOSED
